  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc / 0.659 F1, which beats the best RNA-only (config_006, 0.653) by ~3.5%. The key open question is whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) meaningfully affects performance, since we only have one multimodal data point. Config_033 is a clean single-variable A/B comparison with config_032 (only fusion changes from concat to weighted). If weighted fusion improves accuracy, it reveals that modality importance is asymmetric and learnable, guiding future fusion design. If it does not, it confirms concat is sufficient and directs budget toward other levers (e.g., image encoder choice or aggregation). This is the most informative next step because it isolates one design decision at the current best-performing operating point, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

